格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Claude Code for dsh (DeepSeek Harness): runs your logged-in Claude Code CLI as a model provider, with live models, session resume, approvals, rewind, memory and remote SSH workspaces","id":"gh:1366664192","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-oh-my-claude","slug":"lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude","topics":["anthropic","claude","claude-code","claude-code-cli","claude-subscription","cordis","deepseek","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-claude","dsh-plugin","dsh-provider","llm-provider","typescript"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Claude Code for dsh (DeepSeek Harness): runs your logged-in Claude Code CLI as a model provider, wit"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"h live models, session resume, approvals, rewind, memory and remote SSH workspaces"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"Oh My Claude"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Claude Code, native inside dsh"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Drive your logged-in Claude Code CLI as a first-class dsh provider: no API key, no extra services, n"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"o runtime dependencies."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Built with AI assistance, and open to more. Contributions from AI coding agents are welcome; start w"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"ith CONTRIBUTING.md."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Claude Code CLI as an LLM provider for dsh. Every request drives `claude -p` with stream-json in and"},{"id":"p7s2","text":" out, so it uses whatever login, hooks, CLAUDE.md files, MCP servers and rate limits Claude Code alr"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"eady has. No API key needed. The plugin speaks the CLI's own protocol (the one the Agent SDK wraps) "},{"id":"p7s4","text":"directly, so it has no runtime dependencies."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Tour"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"The shield is dsh's own control. In a Claude session its rows become Claude's six permission modes, "},{"id":"p9s2","text":"each labelled with the dsh access level it sets underneath."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"dsh ships prereleases only and moves client APIs between them, so every release of the plugin record"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"s the dsh line it was written for and the dsh it was driven on. \"Runs on\" is the range the code carr"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"ies branches for; \"tested on\" is the dsh installed on the box when the release was cut. The update p"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"ill reads the floor off the registry: a box whose dsh is below it is never offered the update comman"},{"id":"p12s5","text":"d, and the pill names the dsh that release needs instead."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"| Plugin | Runs on dsh | Tested on dsh | npm tag |"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"| 1.6.0 | 0.2.2-alpha.2 through 0.2.2-rc.1 | 0.2.2-rc.1 | `latest` |\n| 1.5.14 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0"},{"id":"p14s2","text":".2.2-rc.1 | 0.2.2-rc.1 | `dsh-0.2.1`, `dsh-0.2` |\n| 1.5.13 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.2-rc.1 | 0.2.2-r"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"c.1 | none, superseded by 1.5.14 |\n| 1.5.12 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.2-alpha.2 | 0.2.2-alpha.2 | non"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"e, superseded by 1.5.13 |\n| 1.5.11 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.2-alpha.2 | 0.2.2-alpha.2 | none, supers"},{"id":"p14s5","text":"eded by 1.5.12 |\n| 1.5.10 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.2-alpha.2 | 0.2.2-alpha.2 | none, superseded by 1"},{"id":"p14s6","text":".5.11 |\n| 1.5.9 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.1-rc.4 | 0.2.1-rc.4 | none, superseded by 1.5.10 |\n| 1.5.8 "},{"id":"p14s7","text":"| 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.1-rc.4 | 0.2.1-rc.4 | none, superseded by 1.5.9 |\n| 1.5.7 | 0.2.0-rc.1 thro"},{"id":"p14s8","text":"ugh 0.2.1-rc.3 | 0.2.1-rc.3 | none, superseded by 1.5.8 |\n| 1.5.6 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.1-rc.3 | "},{"id":"p14s9","text":"0.2.1-rc.3 | none, superseded by 1.5.7 |\n| 1.5.5 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.1-rc.2 | 0.2.1-rc.2 | none"},{"id":"p14s10","text":", superseded by 1.5.6 |\n| 1.5.4 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.1-rc.2 | 0.2.1-rc.2 | none, superseded by 1"},{"id":"p14s11","text":".5.5 |\n| 1.5.3 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.1-alpha.1 | 0.2.1-alpha.1 | none, superseded by 1.5.4 |\n| 1."},{"id":"p14s12","text":"5.2 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.0-rc.2 | 0.2.0-rc.2 | none, superseded by 1.5.3 |\n| 1.4.2 | 0.1.5-rc.1 "},{"id":"p14s13","text":"through 0.1.7-rc.2 | 0.1.7-rc.2 | `dsh-0.1.7` |\n| 1.4.1 | 0.1.5-rc.1 through 0.1.7-rc.2 | 0.1.7-rc.2"},{"id":"p14s14","text":" | none, superseded by 1.4.2 |\n| 1.4.0 | 0.1.5-rc.1 through 0.1.7-rc.2 | 0.1.7-rc.2 | none, supersed"},{"id":"p14s15","text":"ed by 1.4.1 |\n| 1.3.1 | 0.1.5-rc.1 through 0.1.6-alpha.2 | 0.1.6-alpha.2 | `dsh-0.1.6` |\n| 1.2.1 | 0"},{"id":"p14s16","text":".1.5-rc.1 through 0.1.6-alpha.2 | 0.1.6-alpha.2 | `dsh-0.1.5` |"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## What you get"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"1. Any Claude model your login can use, in dsh's own picker. Hide the ones you don't use with a swit"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"ch in Settings, or with `hiddenModels` in the plugin config. Models\n2. Every dsh session resumes its"},{"id":"p16s3","text":" Claude Code session, tool history included, and a terminal `claude /resume` sees the same one. Sess"},{"id":"p16s4","text":"ions\n3. Restart dsh without killing a running Claude turn. Restarts\n4. dsh's access shield sets Clau"},{"id":"p16s5","text":"de's six permission modes per session. Permission mode\n5. Claude's permission prompts, questions and"},{"id":"p16s6","text":" plan reviews become dsh dialogs, each option's preview under the question. Approvals\n6. One spark b"},{"id":"p16s7","text":"utton opens Memory, Rewind, Changes, MCP and seven more tabs, all reachable from the keyboard. The p"},{"id":"p16s8","text":"anel\n7. Cost and cached tokens in dsh's footer, with a spend line that turns the pill orange. Cost p"},{"id":"p16s9","text":"ill\n8. Plan usage (5-hour, weekly, extra usage) in dsh's context ring, which turns amber near a limi"},{"id":"p16s10","text":"t and red at one, with a notice above the composer. Only limits the session's model counts against, "},{"id":"p16s11","text":"graded by Anthropic, so a new model needs no update. Plan usage\n9. Restore or import any past Claude"},{"id":"p16s12","text":" transcript, from dsh or from a terminal, and search inside them for what was said. Session browser\n"},{"id":"p16s13","text":"10. Claude's slash commands and skills show up in dsh's slash menu under their own names, as `/claud"},{"id":"p16s14","text":"e-<name>` where dsh already uses the name. A skill dsh also serves runs on any model, and so does on"},{"id":"p16s15","text":"e only Claude Code has: typed in a session on another model, it goes to that model with its instruct"},{"id":"p16s16","text":"ions (switch it off in Settings). Command bridge\n11. Claude gets dsh's subagents, jobs, goals and we"},{"id":"p16s17","text":"b search over MCP. dsh tools over MCP\n12. Edit CLAUDE.md, settings.json and MCP servers from the pan"},{"id":"p16s18","text":"el, on this box or a remote one, and sign in to an MCP server that needs it. Instructions, settings."},{"id":"p16s19","text":"json editor, MCP\n13. Run Claude on another box over SSH, or mount several accounts. Remote boxes and"},{"id":"p16s20","text":" accounts\n14. Report a problem with a redacted box report, copied or filed as an issue. Report a pro"},{"id":"p16s21","text":"blem\n15. All the orange is a switch, per group, any colour. Claude look\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## What it touches"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"- **Runs** the `claude` binary you already have, on this box or on one you add over SSH.\n- **Reads**"},{"id":"p18s2","text":" Claude Code's login (`~/.claude/.credentials.json`, on macOS the `Claude Code-credentials` Keychain"},{"id":"p18s3","text":" entry when that file has no live token, or `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` when set) to fetch the model list an"},{"id":"p18s4","text":"d your plan usage. That token goes only to `api.anthropic.com`.\n- **Writes** its own state under `~/"},{"id":"p18s5","text":".local/state/dsh-oh-my-claude/`; login tokens for SSH boxes are files only you can read. CLAUDE.md, "},{"id":"p18s6","text":"settings.json and MCP servers change only when you edit them from the panel.\n- **Listens** on a Unix"},{"id":"p18s7","text":" socket for the keeper that holds Claude across a dsh restart. Its HTTP routes live inside dsh's own"},{"id":"p18s8","text":" server, so on DSH Web it opens no TCP port. Under DSH Desktop, whose web server answers 403 to anyt"},{"id":"p18s9","text":"hing but its own window, the bridge that hands dsh's tools to Claude also listens on 127.0.0.1, behi"},{"id":"p18s10","text":"nd the same key.\n- **Calls out** to `api.anthropic.com` (models, plan usage), `status.anthropic.com`"},{"id":"p18s11","text":", `downloads.claude.ai` (the CLI's release pointer), `registry.npmjs.org` (plugin update check) and "},{"id":"p18s12","text":"`api.github.com` (the repo's star count). SSH goes only to boxes you add."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
